<body>
<div class="page">
  <div class="bar">
    <a class="home" href="https://charlietrenorden.com/"><span class="back">&larr;</span>&nbsp;Other projects</a>
    <button class="toggle" id="themeBtn" type="button" aria-label="Toggle light and dark theme"><span class="dot"></span><span id="themeLbl">Dark</span></button>
  </div>

  <header class="hero">
    <h1>Shortfall</h1>
    <p class="lede">Six accounting tests over the S&amp;P 500 and the ASX&nbsp;200.
    Each company is scored 0-100 on its worst two. <strong>Higher means further into
    the tail</strong>, against peers in the same sector.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="panel" id="quadPanel" aria-label="Score against short interest">
    <div class="panel-head">
      <h2>Compare any two</h2>
      <label class="xpick"><select id="yvar"></select> against <select id="xvar"></select></label>
      <p class="note" id="quadNote"></p>
    </div>
    <svg id="quadSvg" role="img" aria-label="Score against short interest"></svg>
    <p class="chartkey" id="quadKey"></p>

  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="stripPanel" aria-label="Where each company sits on each test">
    <div class="panel-head">
      <h2>Test by test</h2>
      <p class="note" id="stripNote"></p>
    </div>
    <div id="strips"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="weights">
    <div class="panel-head">
      <h2>Weighting</h2>
      <p class="note">Weighted by how directly each test observes an accounting
      problem, not equally. Cards show the default score when you move them.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="sliders"></div>
    <button id="resetWeights" type="button">Reset</button>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="filterPanel">
    <div id="filters"></div>
  </section>

  <nav class="pager top" id="pagerTop" aria-label="Result pages">
    <button type="button" id="prevPageTop" aria-label="Previous page">&larr;</button>
    <span id="pageInfoTop"></span>
    <button type="button" id="nextPageTop" aria-label="Next page">&rarr;</button>
  </nav>

  <div id="testHead" aria-label="Filter each test"></div>

  <section id="cards"></section>

  <nav class="pager" id="pager" aria-label="Result pages">
    <button type="button" id="prevPage" aria-label="Previous page">&larr;</button>
    <span id="pageInfo"></span>
    <button type="button" id="nextPage" aria-label="Next page">&rarr;</button>
  </nav>

  <div id="tip" role="tooltip"></div>

  <section class="panel" id="explain">
    <h2>The six tests</h2>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Test</th>
            <th>Measures</th>
            <th>The worry</th>
            <th>The innocent reading</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody id="explainBody"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="limits">
    <h2>Caveats</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No backtest.</strong> Nobody knows whether these tests predict anything.
      Score against 12-month return is rho 0.01 - but that is not evidence they fail
      either. One year of 656 names cannot detect an effect the size the academic work
      on accruals reports. It would take a decade of point-in-time cross-sections and
      decile portfolio sorts to answer the question at all.</li>
      <li><strong>The tests miss the known cases.</strong> The {{ disclosed|length }}
      companies that restated, changed auditor or filed late sit at a median rank of
      291 of {{ names|length }} - no higher than everyone else. Short sellers spotted
      them (5.4% of float against 3.5%); these tests did not.</li>
      <li><strong>Filing events are US only.</strong> {{ counts.get("Australia (ASX)", 0) }}
      Australian names cannot carry them.</li>
      <li><strong>Australian cash flow is derived.</strong> Two routes; where they
      disagree the accruals flag is dropped, not guessed.</li>
      <li><strong>Inventory is scaled by revenue,</strong> not cost of sales, which is not
      reliably tagged.</li>
      <li><strong>{{ excluded|length }} companies are unranked,</strong> with fewer than
      three applicable tests. Not applicable never means a pass.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="fineprint">SEC EDGAR for the United States, Yahoo Finance for Australia,
    as filed. Not investment advice.</p>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <a href="https://charlietrenorden.com/">charlietrenorden.com</a>
  </footer>
